    "details": "The Angie Software Team reports:\n\n> When using an OpenSSL version without native HTTP/3 support (3.5.0 or\n> earlier), if the default server for the address that accepted a\n> regular HTTPS request also used HTTP/3 (the listen directive with the\n> quic parameter, possibly on a different port), while a server block\n> without HTTP/3 was selected by domain name (SNI), limited worker\n> process memory corruption or a worker process crash could occur\n> (CVE-2026-90439); the fix was ported from nginx 1.31.6.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0464",
